# OpenSpec + Git (LSI)

**Canonical overlay:** [`.lsi/workflows/openspec-git-integration.md`](../../.lsi/workflows/openspec-git-integration.md)

OpenSpec changes under `openspec/changes/<change-slug>/` define **what to build**. Trello + branch id define **delivery tracking**.

**Branch policy:** [`.cursor/rules/branch-workflow.mdc`](branch-workflow.mdc) — do not duplicate protected-branch refusal here.

## Workflow commands

**OpenSpec:** `/opsx:explore`, `/opsx:propose`, `/opsx:apply`, `/opsx:sync`, `/opsx:archive`

**LSI (git):** `/lsi:help`, `/lsi:card`, `/lsi:card-link`, `/lsi:trello-list`, `/lsi:trello-branch`, `/lsi:branch`, `/lsi:senior`, `/lsi:commit`, `/lsi:readiness`, `/lsi:review`, `/lsi:pr`, `/lsi:promote`, `/lsi:merge-desc`, `/lsi:close`, address-*, adopt-*, release-train family, `/lsi:version`, `/lsi:changelog`, `/lsi:release`, `/lsi:bootstrap-release`, `/lsi:update`

| Step | Command |
|------|---------|
| Explore | `/opsx:explore` |
| Propose | `/opsx:propose` |
| Card + branch | `/lsi:card` (from `main` or `staging`) |
| Link card to existing branch | `/lsi:card-link` (on feature branch without Trello id) |
| List / branch from To Do card | `/lsi:trello-list` (picker; confirm → `git tb`), `/lsi:trello-branch` (from `main`/`staging`) |
| Senior analysis | `/lsi:senior` (large changes) |
| Mode A PR | `/lsi:pr` mode A (`openspec/` only) |
| Implement | `/opsx:apply` (bot lane) |
| Commit | `/lsi:commit` (when asked) |
| Pre-PR | `/lsi:readiness` then `/lsi:review` for Mode A/B/C (separate; not inside `/lsi:pr`; bots nest readiness) |
| Mode B PR | `/lsi:pr` mode B → `staging` |
| Promote to main | `/lsi:promote` (change still active) |
| Close after promote | `/lsi:close` on **`main`** only after promotion merges |
| Merge desc | `/lsi:merge-desc` |
| Release | `/lsi:version`, `/lsi:changelog`, `/lsi:release`, `/lsi:release-train`, `/lsi:bootstrap-release` — **`main` only**; never nest in other commands |

## Before implementation

1. Confirm ticket branch with Trello id + OpenSpec slug suffix.
2. Read `proposal.md`, `design.md`, delta specs for active change.
3. **`tasks.md` must not** list administrative lifecycle work (close/sync/archive, promote, release-train family, `/lsi:update`, meta process) — only purpose-fulfilling apply work. `/lsi:readiness` enforces this.

## Commits and PRs

- On commit requests: `/lsi:commit` — plan from `tasks.md` sections.
- On PR prep: `/lsi:readiness` then `/lsi:review` before `/lsi:pr` (do not chain inside `/lsi:pr`).
- PR **Related:** `openspec/changes/<slug>/` + Trello card id.
- Do not auto-commit or auto-open PRs.
- When policy is ambiguous, ask one focused question before proceeding.
- Command Output is verify-shaped; no `Next:` footers — sequencing lives in the lifecycle + bot playbook.

See [openspec-git-integration.md § Full lifecycle](../../.lsi/workflows/openspec-git-integration.md).
